WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.848
CVE2 cleanly separates family from core.

2
00:00:03.848 --> 00:00:09.234
OpenHW forked Ibex in 2023 and named the code base CVE2.

3
00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:17.988
Its current named core, CV32E20, targets constrained 32-bit MCU and embedded subsystem use.

4
00:00:17.988 --> 00:00:27.703
Stage one fetches instructions; stage two combines decode, register access, execution, and writeback.

5
00:00:27.703 --> 00:00:36.360
The specification defines golden RV32E M C and RV32I M C builds for FPGA and ASIC targets.

6
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:42.420
The part number alone cannot carry those configuration choices.

